IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-schedule-three`

-- ind-c-tests-schedule.l4: independent tests (ind-c) of s.41 and the Third Schedule.
-- Every expected value was decided from the gazette (Sefer HaChukim 3349, p. 193 for s.41, p. 205 for the
-- Third Schedule) before the encoding was opened; the scenario ids are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md.

§ `ind-c: s 41 and the Third Schedule`

§§ `Fixtures`

`an individual violator` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "ind-1", `kind of person` IS `an individual`
`a corporate violator` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "corp-1", `kind of person` IS `a corporation`

GIVEN who IS A Person
      what IS A `Listed violation`
GIVETH A Violation
`ind-c violation by` who `of` what MEANS
    Violation WITH `the violator` IS who
                 , `the listed violation` IS what
                 , `reference for the act` IS "act-1"
                 , `date of the act` IS YMD 2027 3 10

§§ `A1-A7: column B, fourteen cells (gazette p. 205)`

-- A1, item (1): individual 20,000; corporation a dash.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `work with no licence at all` EQUALS JUST 20000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `work with no licence at all` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A2, item (2): individual 10,000; corporation a dash.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system` EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A3, item (3): 5,000 / 10,000.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind` EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind` EQUALS JUST 10000
-- A4, item (4): 20,000; corporation a dash.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `installation without the tightness test of the piping` EQUALS JUST 20000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `installation without the tightness test of the piping` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A5, item (5): 20,000 / 40,000.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `engaging a person who had no licence at all` EQUALS JUST 20000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `engaging a person who had no licence at all` EQUALS JUST 40000
-- A6, item (6): 10,000 / 20,000.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind` EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind` EQUALS JUST 20000
-- A7, item (7): 3,000 / 6,000.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded` EQUALS JUST 3000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded` EQUALS JUST 6000

-- The same cells through the exported amount function, which takes a whole Violation.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `work with no licence at all`) EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind`) EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `engaging a person who had no licence at all`) EQUALS 40000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded`) EQUALS 3000
-- A dash yields no amount: my expectation accepts NOTHING or REFUSE, and never a number.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `work with no licence at all`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `installation without the tightness test of the piping`)

§§ `A12-A14: routes into the Schedule (which item a set of facts reaches)`

-- A12: a grade 1 holder working on a 50 kW system is item (2); A13: no licence at all is item (1);
-- A14: an operator employing a grade 2 holder on a system above 70 kW is item (6), no licence at all item (5).
-- The encoding receives the item as an input (`Listed violation`), so these test the provision each item names.
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system` EQUALS `contravenes section 3(a)`
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `work with no licence at all` EQUALS `contravenes section 3(a)`
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind` EQUALS `contravenes section 4`
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `installation without the tightness test of the piping` EQUALS `contravenes section 13`
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `engaging a person who had no licence at all` EQUALS `contravenes section 18(a)`
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind` EQUALS `contravenes section 18(a)`
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded` EQUALS `contravenes section 31(2)`
#ASSERT (`Third Schedule — the row for` `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`)'s `the item number` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT (`Third Schedule — the row for` `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`)'s `the item number` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT count `the Third Schedule` EQUALS 7

§§ `s 41(a): the Commissioner's power, gated by Chapter 6 and the authorisation`

-- An individual's item (1): Chapter 6 in force and the Commissioner authorised: a sanction may be imposed.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`ind-c violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `work with no licence at all`) TRUE TRUE
-- G5 (with s.41): Chapter 6 not in force on the day of the act: no sanction.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`ind-c violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `work with no licence at all`) FALSE TRUE)
-- Not a Commissioner authorised for Chapter 6: no sanction.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`ind-c violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `work with no licence at all`) TRUE FALSE)
-- A corporation's item (3) has an amount: a sanction may be imposed.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`ind-c violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind`) TRUE TRUE
-- A1/A2/A4 corporation, "may a sanction be imposed?": my expectation is FALSE; the encoding refuses.  Those
-- assertions are in ind-c-tests-disagree.l4.  The encoding's alternative reading of the dash answers FALSE:
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(a) — reading a dash as no sanction, a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`ind-c violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `work with no licence at all`) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(a) — reading a dash as no sanction, a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`ind-c violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `installation without the tightness test of the piping`) TRUE TRUE)
-- Chapter 6 not in force wins before the dash is reached.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`ind-c violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `work with no licence at all`) FALSE TRUE)

§§ `B: s 41(b), the Minister's order and its cap (gazette p. 193)`

GIVEN individual IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      corporation IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Third Schedule row`
`ind-c an order setting item (3) to` individual `and` corporation MEANS
    LIST (`Third Schedule row` WITH `the item number` IS 3
                                  , `the listed violation` IS `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind`
                                  , `the provision contravened` IS `contravenes section 4`
                                  , `column B for an individual` IS individual
                                  , `column B for a corporation` IS corporation)

-- B1: an individual amount of exactly 40,000, both approvals: permitted.
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` (`ind-c an order setting item (3) to` (JUST 40000) `and` (JUST 10000)) TRUE TRUE
-- B2: 40,001: not permitted.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` (`ind-c an order setting item (3) to` (JUST 40001) `and` (JUST 10000)) TRUE TRUE)
-- B3: a corporation amount of exactly 80,000: permitted.
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` (`ind-c an order setting item (3) to` (JUST 5000) `and` (JUST 80000)) TRUE TRUE
-- B4: 80,001: not permitted.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` (`ind-c an order setting item (3) to` (JUST 5000) `and` (JUST 80001)) TRUE TRUE)
-- B5: a corporation amount of 50,000 (above the individual cap, below the corporation cap): permitted.
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` (`ind-c an order setting item (3) to` (JUST 5000) `and` (JUST 50000)) TRUE TRUE
-- B6: no consent of the Minister of Justice: not permitted.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` (`ind-c an order setting item (3) to` (JUST 10000) `and` (JUST 10000)) FALSE TRUE)
-- B7: no approval of the Labour and Welfare Committee: not permitted.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` (`ind-c an order setting item (3) to` (JUST 10000) `and` (JUST 10000)) TRUE FALSE)
-- The Schedule as enacted is within the cap.
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — every row is within the cap` `the Third Schedule`
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the cap on a column B amount for` `an individual` EQUALS 40000
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the cap on a column B amount for` `a corporation` EQUALS 80000
